From: ON-FireLOS
Subject: [PATCH] f2fs: also write a clean checkpoint on umount

After the sync before every shutdown the file system is clean, and
f2fs_put_super no longer wrote a checkpoint. The last one carried no
umount flag, and fsck.f2fs took every reboot for a power failure.
Only helps if /data can actually be unmounted at shutdown.
Corresponds to upstream "f2fs: write checkpoint before put_super" (Linux 4.2).
---
diff -ru a/fs/f2fs/checkpoint.c b/fs/f2fs/checkpoint.c
--- a/fs/f2fs/checkpoint.c	2026-10-29 04:08:38.450237907 +0000
+++ b/fs/f2fs/checkpoint.c	2026-10-29 04:08:38.450452638 +0000
@@ -996,7 +996,8 @@
 
 	mutex_lock(&sbi->cp_mutex);
 
-	if (!sbi->s_dirty && cpc->reason != CP_DISCARD)
+	if (!sbi->s_dirty && cpc->reason != CP_DISCARD &&
+			cpc->reason != CP_UMOUNT)
 		goto out;
 	if (unlikely(f2fs_cp_error(sbi)))
 		goto out;
diff -ru a/fs/f2fs/super.c b/fs/f2fs/super.c
--- a/fs/f2fs/super.c	2026-10-29 04:08:38.449839645 +0000
+++ b/fs/f2fs/super.c	2026-10-29 04:08:38.450152466 +0000
@@ -435,8 +435,14 @@
 	f2fs_destroy_stats(sbi);
 	stop_gc_thread(sbi);
 
-	/* We don't need to do checkpoint when it's clean */
-	if (sbi->s_dirty) {
+	/*
+	 * We don't need to do checkpoint when it's clean - unless the last
+	 * one lacks the umount flag. Android syncs before every shutdown,
+	 * which writes a checkpoint without it; fsck then took every reboot
+	 * for a power loss and checked all of /data (upstream since 4.2).
+	 */
+	if (sbi->s_dirty ||
+			!is_set_ckpt_flags(F2FS_CKPT(sbi), CP_UMOUNT_FLAG)) {
 		struct cp_control cpc = {
 			.reason = CP_UMOUNT,
 		};
